  "conventions": [
    "The initial package is paid at the review date for discounting; subsequent operating cash is assumed at each annual period end.",
    "Net product sales are commercializer net receipts, not patient retail price. Royalty vehicles receive only the specified spread.",
    "100% vehicle ownership; negative annual operating cash is a new contribution; positive cash is distributed after a 25% planning reserve, with no recycling or tax-loss benefit.",
    "Five years is a comparison convention, not an investor-specified deadline. Ten-year cases extend only a branch already launched by year 5.",
    "For the ten-year sensitivity, a year-5 25% ramp becomes 60% in year 6 and 100% from year 7. Other launched branches are at 100% from year 6. Listed fixed costs stay nominally constant, with no new development or application fee; prices then either stay fixed or erode 10% annually.",
    "Ten-year continuation does not establish rights duration, patent protection, survival, actual pricing or funding. No terminal sale value or inventory salvage is counted.",
    "Annual cash aggregation cannot fully capture intra-year working capital, minimum orders or collection delays. Additional financing needs would increase contributions.",
